fact WorkItem(id: "WI-439", description: some(value: "Iterable.filter member (WI-424 pattern): derived combinator via iterator(c) — 'operation filter(c: C, pred: Function[Element, Bool, E]) -> Stream[Element, E] = FilteredStream.filter(iterator(c), pred)' (or the filtered(...) constructor directly; inner call MUST be qualified/foreign — the WI-411 short-name hazard, same as find/map). Engine = the delivered FilteredStream lazy carrier (WI-410/413). Same mechanism as WI-424 find/map: enclosing-sort param rigidification + carrier-param receiver + provision-written E threading. NOTE the current-pattern limitation to document in a comment: tying pred's row to the collection's access row E forces a PURE pred for List (E = {}); the decoupled arrow form is WI-441. ACCEPTANCE: filter on List evaluates (keep/drop/laziness), typechecks pure, wrong-element pred rejected; parity tests vs Stream-level filter; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-11T15:05:24Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-439", author: "user", content: "Delivered b2e55df. Two gaps SURFACED by the tests, out of this WI's acceptance scope: (1) SYNTHESIS GAP — collect's Elem does not ground from a member result whose Element comes from a CONCRETE provision binding (BoxColl 'Element = Int64' fails 'expected a type for Elem, got unconstrained') while the GENERIC List provision (Element = T) grounds fine; suspect the WI-391 Ref-vs-nullary-Fn provides-lowering divergence — root-cause alongside WI-391; workaround in test = explicit collect[Elem, Eff] bindings. (2) PARSE GAP — qualified call with explicit type-arg brackets, e.g. FilteredStream.filter[S = Int64, Eff = {}](...), is a syntax error; only the unqualified-import form takes brackets; relates WI-311 (application/name grammar merge). Laziness not separately asserted — it is the delivered FilteredStream engine's property (WI-410/413 tests).", at: "2026-06-11T15:05:23Z")
